.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt ESPI 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm espi
.Nd AMD FCH eSPI controller nexus driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /devices/ Ns Ar fch Ns Pa @0,0/espi@ Ns Ar n
.Pp
.Pa /devices/ Ns Ar fch Ns Pa @0,0/espi@ Ns Ar n Ns Pa :ctl
.Pp
.In sys/espi_ctl.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver attaches to the Enhanced Serial Peripheral Interface
.Pq eSPI
controllers in the Fusion Controller Hub
.Pq FCH
of AMD Zen processors.
The controllers appear as children of the FCH node,
.Ar fch ,
which is named after the FCH model
.Pq huashan, songshan or kunlun ,
with the controller number
.Ar n
as the unit address.
.Pp
An eSPI controller communicates with a single target device over up to four
channels.
These are the peripheral channel, the virtual wire channel, the out-of-band
message channel and the flash access channel.
The
.Nm
driver is a nexus driver.
Its children are the drivers for the channels that the controller's target
provides, and each child has the channel number as its unit address.
.Pp
The board's platform data determines how each controller is used.
A controller that connects the processor to the service processor is used by
the operating system itself from early in boot, and the
.Nm
driver attaches to it passively.
In that mode it maps the controller's registers and reports its state, but
issues no commands and has no children.
A controller that the platform data assigns to this driver is reset and
configured by it.
A controller with no target behind it does not attach.
.Pp
The following children may be created:
.Bl -tag -width "espi_flash(4D)"
.It Xr espi_flash 4D
Provides access to a flash device attached to the target over the flash access
channel.
It is created only when that channel was enabled.
.El
.Sh PROPERTIES
The driver records what it finds out about the controller, the link and the
target as properties on its node, which can be read with
.Xr prtconf 8 .
They are informational and cannot be set.
.Bl -tag -width Sy
.It Sy espi-role
How the platform uses the controller, one of
.Sy ipcc ,
.Sy nexus
or
.Sy none .
.It Sy espi-mode
Either
.Sy passive
or
.Sy owner ,
as described above.
.It Sy controller-version
The version of the eSPI specification that the controller implements.
.It Sy controller-channels
The channels that the controller supports, from
.Sy peripheral ,
.Sy vwire ,
.Sy oob
and
.Sy flash .
.It Sy init-status
How far the controller's own hardware initialisation sequence got, which
applies to the controller that the system booted through.
It is
.Sy idle
for a controller the firmware did not initialise and
.Sy complete
for one it did, and otherwise names the step at which the sequence stopped.
.It Sy io-mode
The I/O mode in use on the link, one of
.Sy single ,
.Sy dual
or
.Sy quad .
.It Sy clock-frequency
The link clock frequency in Hz.
.It Sy crc-enabled
Whether CRC checking is enabled on the link.
.It Sy alert-mode
How the target signals alerts, either
.Sy in-band
or
.Sy pin .
.It Sy enabled-channels
The channels that are enabled in the controller.
.It Sy pins-muxed
Whether all of the controller's pins are set to their eSPI functions.
The driver sets them in owner mode and only checks them in passive mode.
The property is absent when the driver has no pin data for the processor.
.El
.Pp
When the driver has configured a target itself, it also records:
.Bl -tag -width Sy
.It Sy target-version
The version of the eSPI specification that the target implements.
.It Sy target-channels
The channels that the target supports.
.It Sy flash-payload , flash-max-read
The largest number of bytes in a single flash write request and a single
flash read request.
.It Sy flash-erase-sizes
The erase block sizes that the target advertised, with bit
.Em n
set for 2^n KiB blocks.
.El
.Sh IOCTLS
A controller that the driver has reset and configured itself has a character
device minor node named
.Pa ctl ,
which is a general control interface for the controller and its target.
Only a privileged process in the global zone may open it.
It may be opened with
.Dv O_EXCL
to keep other processes out while a sequence of operations is made.
The ioctls are defined in
.In sys/espi_ctl.h .
.Ss Configuration Registers
The following ioctls give access to the target's configuration registers.
Their argument is a pointer to an
.Vt espi_cfg_t :
.Bd -literal
typedef struct espi_cfg {
	uint32_t	ec_offset;
	uint32_t	ec_value;
} espi_cfg_t;
.Ed
.Pp
.Fa ec_offset
is the offset of a 32-bit register, which must be a multiple of 4 and less than
.Dv ESPI_CFG_SIZE .
Registers from
.Dv ESPI_CFG_PLATFORM_START
are defined by the platform rather than by the eSPI specification.
.Bl -tag -width Dv
.It Dv ESPI_IOC_CFG_READ
Reads the register with a GET_CONFIGURATION command and stores its value in
.Fa ec_value .
.It Dv ESPI_IOC_CFG_WRITE
Writes
.Fa ec_value
to the register with a SET_CONFIGURATION command.
The file descriptor must be open for writing, and the register must be one that
the platform defines.
The registers that the specification defines are configured only by the
driver.
.El
.Sh ARCHITECTURE
The
.Nm
driver is only available on the oxide platform.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /platform/oxide/kernel/drv/amd64/espi
64-bit AMD64 ELF kernel driver
.El
.Sh ERRORS
On failure,
.Va errno
is set to indicate the error.
The more common errors are listed below.
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Dv ESPI_IOC_CFG_WRITE
was requested on a file descriptor that is not open for writing.
.It Er EBUSY
The device is already open and
.Dv O_EXCL
was requested, or it is open with
.Dv O_EXCL ,
or the eSPI controller could not accept a command.
.It Er EFAULT
The driver could not copy data to or from the address space of the calling
process.
.It Er EINVAL
The register offset is not aligned or is beyond the configuration space.
.It Er ENXIO
The controller is not one that the driver configured, or no target is present.
.It Er EPERM
The caller lacks the privilege to open the device, or
.Dv ESPI_IOC_CFG_WRITE
named a register that the eSPI specification defines.
.It Er ETIMEDOUT
The target did not complete a command in time.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
.Sy Uncommitted
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr espi_flash 4D
.Rs
.%Q Intel Corporation
.%T Enhanced Serial Peripheral Interface (eSPI) Interface Base Specification (for Client and Server Platforms)
.%N 327432-005 Revision 1.5
.%D May 2022
.Re
